Ladybird stops propagation from <body> to the viewport when <html> or
<body> is a size or inline-size container, since container-type then
applies style containment to it. Blink does the same, because its
StyleResolver::ShouldStopBodyPropagation() checks the effective
containment, which ComputedStyle::EffectiveContainment() computes from
ContainerType() as well as Contain(). Gecko’s nsCSSFrameConstructor
checks nsStyleDisplay::IsContainAny(), the effective containment that
its style adjuster sets from container-type as well. And WebKit checks
usedContain().isNone() in its StyleAdjuster before propagating, where
ComputedStyle::usedContain() adds style plus size or inline-size
containment for container-type.
